WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:07.400
In April 2027, the National Army Museum opens
«Uniform: Identity and Innovation».

2
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:12.700
We would build it off site, and have it assembled
in the gallery by 12 February.

3
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:18.000
A central «Y» of curved setworks divides
the gallery into three colours.

4
00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:20.900
Dark blue, where the visit begins.

5
00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:26.000
Lime green, for uniforms in tall cases
and framed graphic panels.

6
00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:29.300
And rust, around the three-sided setworks.

7
00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:35.300
Nine inset cases sit flush in the walls,
behind 12 mm acrylic.

8
00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:41.200
Eight hooded cases, with mitred acrylic hoods
and Oddy-tested seals.

9
00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:45.600
And case 3F, large enough for a full battledress.

10
00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:49.500
An interactive table, built to the designer’s drawing.

11
00:00:50.410 --> 00:00:54.500
Everything is made in our workshop in Setúbal,
from formaldehyde-free board.

12
00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:58.100
Finished, and left to off-gas before it travels.

13
00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:01.900
Delivered on Mondays, in modules sized for the lift.

14
00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:06.300
Installed with no hot works,
and the collection protected.

15
00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:11.500
Handed over clean, ready for your exhibits,
AV and graphics.

16
00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:17.000
«Uniform». Built by Active Reflex and 4x4 Multitrabalhos.
